      description: 'MDAL (Master Data Access Layer), introduced in 2022, facilitates efficient data retrieval and management across distributed systems within the Temenos modular architecture. It provides a structured and flexible approach to accessing external data sources, enabling seamless integration within larger banking applications. MDAL is composed of Data Access Components (modular units encapsulating data access operations), Request Registry (API gateway for mapping requests), and Master Data Access Handler (configurable in Embedded, Inline, or Pre-composed modes). MDAL integrates smoothly with microservices architecture, treating each Data Access Component as a potential microservice for independent deployment and scaling.',
